Subject: [PATCH] device: raise LE security when the device asks, not on connect

With an LTK, device_attach_att() raised the ATT channel's security as soon as
it connected, and device_connect_le() connected at medium security, so
encryption started 26 ms into the connection. On the RG35XX SP (RTL8821CS on
UART), a Backbone Pro controller never answered that encryption request: it
kept sending unencrypted L2CAP data and the link hit its supervision timeout,
every time it reconnected. Encryption that started after the connection
parameter and data length updates, about half a second in, always worked.

Leave the level low and let a read the device refuses as unencrypted raise
it, which shared/att.c already does.
---
--- a/src/device.c
+++ b/src/device.c
@@ -6438,18 +6438,14 @@
 		return false;
 	}
 
-	if (sec_level == BT_IO_SEC_LOW && dev->le_state.paired) {
-		DBG("Elevating security level since LTK is available");
-
-		sec_level = BT_IO_SEC_MEDIUM;
-		bt_io_set(io, &gerr, BT_IO_OPT_SEC_LEVEL, sec_level,
-							BT_IO_OPT_INVALID);
-		if (gerr) {
-			error("bt_io_set: %s", gerr->message);
-			g_error_free(gerr);
-			return false;
-		}
-	}
+	/*
+	 * Not raised here even with an LTK: encryption then starts within
+	 * 30 ms of the connection, and an RTL8821CS controller with a Backbone
+	 * Pro never completes it and loses the link. A read the device refuses
+	 * unencrypted raises it instead (change_security() in shared/att.c).
+	 */
+	if (sec_level == BT_IO_SEC_LOW && dev->le_state.paired)
+		DBG("LTK available; security raised when the device asks");
 
 	dev->att_mtu = MIN(mtu, btd_opts.gatt_mtu);
 	attrib = g_attrib_new(io,
@@ -6594,10 +6590,8 @@
 	/* Set as initiator */
 	dev->le_state.initiator = true;
 
-	if (dev->le_state.paired)
-		sec_level = BT_IO_SEC_MEDIUM;
-	else
-		sec_level = BT_IO_SEC_LOW;
+	/* Low even when paired: see device_attach_att(). */
+	sec_level = BT_IO_SEC_LOW;
 
 	/*
 	 * This connection will help us catch any PDUs that comes before
